From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 16:01:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 012/117] spi: apple: add T8010 controller support

T8010 uses an older Apple SPI register layout with legacy FIFO status,
descriptor-assisted short transfers and a SmartIO-backed transmit path.
The physical input clock and requested speed determine its divider; the
controller requires a minimum divider of two.

Add a T8010 hardware description and implement its PIO and transmit-DMA
paths through transfer_one().  This keeps message sequencing, GPIO chip
select handling, actual_length accounting, DMA mapping and cache
synchronization in the SPI core.  Fall back to PIO when no mapped transmit
scatterlist is available.

Select descriptors solely from generic transfer shape and word width.
There is no Z2 command recognition or touchscreen protocol state in the
controller driver.  Existing non-T8010 controllers retain their original
transfer path.  Add spi-apple.c to the T8010 SPI MAINTAINERS section.

The SPI object and J172 kernel were built with LLVM 18.  A fresh J172 boot
completed firmware upload, created event0 automatically and passed the
DT620 single- and multi-touch test without SPI timeouts.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

